# Comments

`markdoc.config.json` enables `allowComments`, so `<!-- … -->` is a comment.
Tags inside a comment should have no color and no errors.

<!-- {% callout type="bogus" %} A block comment {% /callout %} -->

Inline <!-- {% unknown /%} --> comment.

<!--
{% callout %}
A comment spanning multiple lines.
-->

Tags outside comments keep their colors:

{% callout type="note" %}
A comment inside a tag's body: <!-- {% figure /%} -->
{% /callout %}

## Unclosed comments

An unclosed `<!--` is not a comment (same as Markdoc 0.5), so the tag after it is colored
and validated. The language server should keep running (the bundled Markdoc 0.3 used to hang here).

Typing <!-- here {% figure /%}

## Comment in link text

The server should not hang. Markdoc reports "Can't nest 'comment' in 'link'".

